<h1><span lang="FR">Point Clouds Description</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Point clouds are sets of 3D points generated from scan data, meshes, or other point clouds by sampling. Each entity of this type consists of unconnected <b><a class="glossterm" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1">vertices</a> <span class="glosstext" style="display:'none';" id="POPUP806091253">Each mesh entity consists of vertices that are connected in triangles</span></b>. Point clouds differ from scan data and meshes in that the points are not organised into stripes, patches or triangles.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP224637108" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
