<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image002.jpg" width="635px" height="506px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">Fragment of a point cloud generated from mesh</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Point clouds can be displayed in</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Mode">Points</span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">and</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Mode">Large Points</span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">rendering modes only.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">There are two special types in KUBE that share the same structure as point clouds </span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="text-decoration:none;">Probe Points</span> and Static Stripes.</u> <span lang="EN-GB">They are used in combination with</span> datums <span lang="EN-GB">for checking arm and sensor calibration.</span></p>
